false, "num_turns": 9, "subtype": "success", "api_error_status": null, "result": "I moved the logic into the `salesreport` package. On `sample.csv` the new version prints exactly the same bytes as the old one. Running it with no argument also gives the same usage message and exit code 1.\n\n- `salesreport/loader.py`: reads the CSV.\n- `salesreport/aggregate.py`: the amount calculation, the cancelled check and the grouping are each written once now. The three reports (region, product, month) are listed in one table, `SECTIONS`, that says how to group and sort each one.\n- `salesreport/output.py`: the line format, which was also repeated three times, is now one function.\n- `report.py`: only the entry point is left, 8 lines not counting blank lines and comments.\n\nOne small difference: a bad `qty` or `unit_price` value used to be caught with a bare `except:` and is now caught with `except Exception:`. Output is the same for any normal input. The only change is that pressing Ctrl+C now stops the program instead of being silently treated as 0.", "ttft_ms": 1896, "type": "result", "duration_ms": 30364, "uuid": "73165ad9-daf6-4eb8-aa76-753bc7b1070e", "ttft_stream_ms": 1433, "time_to_request_ms": 280, "time_to_request_phases_ms": {"other": 9, "system_prompt": 14, "resume_other": 0, "process_user_input": 1, "input_attachments": 8, "input_hooks": 2, "transcript_persist": 12, "tool_pool_refresh": 1, "init_message": 5, "engine_pickup": 0, "message_prep": 1, "model_config_wait": 0, "autocompact": 1, "query_setup": 0, "model_gates": 200, "tool_schema_build": 21, "message_normalization": 1, "client_creation": 2, "request_build": 2}, "turn_start_resume_kind": "none", "process_turn_index": 0, "time_to_request_loop_lag_ms": 23, "time_to_request_cpu_ms": 227, "time_to_request_major_faults": 0, "input_attachments_detail": {"slowest_producer": "model", "slowest_producer_ms": 6, "cpu_ms": 11, "major_faults": 0}, "first_content_frame_ms": 1433, "queued_turn_count": 0, "result_index": 0}